  "submitted_text": "Step 1: We need to find the remainder when 2004 is divided by 12. This can be done using the division algorithm which states that for any integers \\(a\\) and \\(b\\), there exist unique integers \\(q\\) (quotient) and \\(r\\) (remainder) such that \\(a = bq + r\\) where \\(0 \\leq r < b\\).\n\nStep 2: Here, \\(a = 2004\\) and \\(b = 12\\). We perform the division \\(2004 \\div 12\\).\n\nStep 3: Calculate the quotient \\(q\\):\n\\[ q = \\left\\lfloor \\frac{2004}{12} \\right\\rfloor = \\left\\lfloor 167 \\right\\rfloor = 167 \\]\n\nStep 4: Calculate the product of the quotient and divisor:\n\\[ 167 \\times 12 = 2004 \\]\n\nStep 5: Subtract this product from the original number to find the remainder:\n\\[ 2004 - 2004 = 0 \\]\n\nFinal answer: \\boxed{0}",
